text: ["({T}: Add {B} or {G}.)\\nAs Overgrown Tomb enters the battlefield, you may pay 2 life. If you don't, it enters the battlefield tapped.", "({T}: Add {B} or {R}.)\\nAs Blood Crypt enters the battlefield, you may pay 2 life. If you don't, it enters the battlefield tapped.", '({T}: Add {B}.)', "({T}: Add {G} or {W}.)\\nAs Temple Garden enters the battlefield, you may pay 2 life. If you don't, it enters the battlefield tapped.", '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {R}.)', "({T}: Add {U} or {R}.)\\nAs Steam Vents enters the battlefield, you may pay 2 life. If you don't, it enters the battlefield tapped.", '({T}: Add {U}.)', "({T}: Add {W} or {U}.)\\nAs Hallowed Fountain enters the battlefield, you may pay 2 life. If you don't, it enters the battlefield tapped.", '({T}: Add {W}.)', "All creatures able to block Golgari Decoy do so.\\nScavenge {3}{G}{G} ({3}{G}{G}, Exile this card from your graveyard: Put a number of +1/+1 counters equal to this card's power on target creature. Scavenge only as a sorcery.)", 'All damage that would be dealt to you and other permanents you control is dealt to Palisade Giant instead.', 'Annihilating Fire deals 3 damage to any target. If a creature dealt damage this way would die this turn, exile it instead.', 'Armory Guard has vigilance as long as you control a Gate.', "As Pithing Needle enters the battlefield, choose a card name.\\nActivated abilities of sources with the chosen name can't be activated unless they're mana abilities.", "As Tablet of the Guilds enters the battlefield, choose two colors.\\nWhenever you cast a spell, if it's at least one of the chosen colors, you gain 1 life for each of the chosen colors it is.", 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a creature.\\nDestroy target creature. Its controller loses 2 life.', "As long as it's not your turn, tapped creatures you control have hexproof.", "At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, if that player has one or fewer cards in hand, they lose 3 life.", "At the beginning of your upkeep, detain target creature an opponent controls. (Until your next turn, that creature can't attack or block and its activated abilities can't be activated.)", "At the beginning of your upkeep, populate. (Create a token that's a copy of a creature token you control.)", "At the beginning of your upkeep, put a filibuster counter on Azor's Elocutors. Then if Azor's Elocutors has five or more filibuster counters on it, you win the game.\\nWhenever a source deals damage to you, remove a filibuster counter from Azor's Elocutors.", 'At the beginning of your upkeep, target opponent reveals the top three cards of their library, may put a creature card from among them onto the battlefield, then puts the rest into their graveyard. You do the same with the top three cards of your library. If two creatures are put onto the battlefield this way, those creatures fight each other.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, you may exchange control of Conjured Currency and target permanent you neither own nor control.', 'Azorius Guildgate enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {U}.', 'Choose one —\\n• All creatures get -1/-1 until end of turn.\\n• Destroy target enchantment.\\n• Regenerate each creature you control.', 'Choose one —\\n• Counter target noncreature spell unless its controller pays {2}.\\n• Izzet Charm deals 2 damage to target creature.\\n• Draw two cards, then discard two cards.', "Choose one —\\n• Creatures you control gain lifelink until end of turn.\\n• Draw a card.\\n• Put target attacking or blocking creature on top of its owner's library.", "Choose one —\\n• Exile target player's graveyard.\\n• Destroy target artifact.\\n• Each creature deals 1 damage to its controller.", 'Choose one —\\n• Target creature gets +2/+2 and gains trample until end of turn.\\n• Exile target creature with power 5 or greater.\\n• Create a 2/2 white Knight creature token with vigilance.', "Counter target creature spell. Essence Backlash deals damage equal to that spell's power to its controller.", 'Counter target instant spell.', "Counter target spell unless its controller pays {X}. If that spell is countered this way, exile it instead of putting it into its owner's graveyard.", 'Counter target spell.', 'Counter target spell. You gain 5 life.', "Create a 1/1 white Bird creature token with flying, then populate. (Create a token that's a copy of a creature token you control.)", "Create a 3/3 green Centaur creature token, then populate. (Create a token that's a copy of a creature token you control.)", 'Create a 3/3 green Centaur creature token.', "Create a 4/4 green Rhino creature token with trample, then populate. (Create a token that's a copy of a creature token you control.)", 'Create an X/X green Ooze creature token.', 'Create four 1/1 red Goblin creature tokens.', 'Creature tokens you control get +1/+1.', "Creatures can't attack you or planeswalkers you control unless their controller pays {X} for each of those creatures, where X is the number of enchantments you control.", 'Creatures you control get +3/+3.', "Deathtouch (Any amount of damage this deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)\\nScavenge {1}{B}{G} ({1}{B}{G}, Exile this card from your graveyard: Put a number of +1/+1 counters equal to this card's power on target creature. Scavenge only as a sorcery.)", "Deathtouch\\nUnleash (You may have this creature enter the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. It can't block as long as it has a +1/+1 counter on it.)", 'Defender, flying', "Defender\\nOgre Jailbreaker can attack as though it didn't have defender as long as you control a Gate.", 'Defender\\nReach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\n{1}{B}{G}: Regenerate Trestle Troll.', 'Defender\\nWhen Gatecreeper Vine enters the battlefield, you may search your library for a basic land card or a Gate card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Defender\\n{2}{U}, {T}: Target player mills X cards, where X is the number of creatures you control with defender.', 'Defender\\n{T}: Add X mana in any combination of colors, where X is the number of creatures with defender you control.', 'Defender\\n{T}: Lobber Crew deals 1 damage to each opponent.\\nWhenever you cast a multicolored spell, untap Lobber Crew.', "Destroy target artifact or enchantment, then populate. (Create a token that's a copy of a creature token you control.)", 'Destroy target artifact you don\'t control.\\nOverload {4}{R} (You may cast this spell for its overload cost. If you do, change "target" in its text to "each.")', 'Destroy target creature or planeswalker.', 'Destroy target creature that dealt damage this turn.', 'Destroy target creature with flying. You gain 2 life.', 'Destroy target creature. Its controller discards a card.', 'Destroy target land. Create a 1/1 red Goblin creature token.', 'Destroy target land. Its controller reveals cards from the top of their library until they reveal a land card, then puts those cards into their graveyard.', 'Destroy target monocolored creature.', "Detain target creature an opponent controls. (Until your next turn, that creature can't attack or block and its activated abilities can't be activated.)\\nDraw a card.", 'Double strike', 'Draw four cards, then discard two cards.', 'Electrickery deals 1 damage to target creature you don\'t control.\\nOverload {1}{R} (You may cast this spell for its overload cost. If you do, change "target" in its text to "each.")', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't attack or block, and its activated abilities can't be activated.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature doesn't untap during its controller's untap step.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1 for each card in its controller's hand.\\nAt the beginning of the draw step of enchanted creature's controller, that player draws an additional card.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1 for each enchantment you control and has first strike.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+1 and has "{R}: This creature gains trample until end of turn."', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2 and has "{U}: This creature gains flying until end of turn."', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets -2/-2.\\nAt the beginning of the upkeep of enchanted creature's controller, that player loses 2 life.", "Enchant creature\\nWhen Knightly Valor enters the battlefield, create a 2/2 white Knight creature token with vigilance. (Attacking doesn't cause it to tap.)\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2 and has vigilance.", 'Enchant land\\nEnchanted land has "Untap this land during each other player\'s untap step."', 'Enchant land\\nEnchanted land has "{T}, Pay 1 life: Draw a card."', 'Enchant land\\nEnchanted land has "{T}: Target creature gains haste until end of turn."', 'Enchant land\\nWhen Security Blockade enters the battlefield, create a 2/2 white Knight creature token with vigilance.\\nEnchanted land has "{T}: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to you this turn."', 'Enchant land\\nWhenever enchanted land becomes tapped, its controller mills three cards.', "Enchant nonland permanent\\nAt the beginning of the upkeep of enchanted permanent's controller, that player sacrifices it unless they pay {X}, where X is its mana value.", 'Equipped creature gets +1/+0 for each of its colors.\\nEquip {1}', "Exile an instant or sorcery spell you control: Put two +1/+1 counters on Nivmagus Elemental. (That spell won't resolve.)", 'Exile target card from a graveyard.\\nDraw a card.', "Exile target creature, then populate. (Create a token that's a copy of a creature token you control.)", "Exile the top X cards of your library. You may cast instant and sorcery spells with mana value X or less from among them without paying their mana costs. Then put all cards exiled this way that weren't cast into your graveyard.", 'Explosive Impact deals 5 damage to any target.', 'First strike, haste', "First strike, haste\\nUnleash (You may have this creature enter the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. It can't block as long as it has a +1/+1 counter on it.)", 'First strike, haste\\nWhenever a player casts a spell from a graveyard, Ash Zealot deals 3 damage to that player.', "First strike\\nUnleash (You may have this creature enter the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. It can't block as long as it has a +1/+1 counter on it.)", 'First strike\\nWhenever Precinct Captain deals combat damage to a player, create a 1/1 white Soldier creature token.', 'First strike\\nWhenever Rakdos Ringleader deals combat damage to a player, that player discards a card at random.\\n{B}: Regenerate Rakdos Ringleader.', 'Flash (You may cast this spell any time you could cast an instant.)\\nFlying', 'Flash (You may cast this spell any time you could cast an instant.)\\nHaste\\n{T}: Izzet Staticaster deals 1 damage to target creature and each other creature with the same name as that creature.', 'Flash (You may cast this spell any time you could cast an instant.)\\nVigilance', 'Flying', 'Flying, haste\\nYou may cast sorcery spells as though they had flash. (You may cast them any time you could cast an instant.)', 'Flying\\nAt the beginning of each combat, any opponent may sacrifice a creature. If a player does, tap Desecration Demon and put a +1/+1 counter on it.', 'Flying\\nDiscard two nonland cards with the same name: Draw four cards.', 'Flying\\nLifelink (Damage dealt by this creature also causes you to gain that much life.)', "Flying\\nSacrifice Judge's Familiar: Counter target instant or sorcery spell unless its controller pays {1}.", "Flying\\nScavenge {2}{B}{B} ({2}{B}{B}, Exile this card from your graveyard: Put a number of +1/+1 counters equal to this card's power on target creature. Scavenge only as a sorcery.)", "Flying\\nUnleash (You may have this creature enter the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. It can't block as long as it has a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\nChaos Imps has trample as long as it has a +1/+1 counter on it.", "Flying\\nWhen Angel of Serenity enters the battlefield, you may exile up to three other target creatures from the battlefield and/or creature cards from graveyards.\\nWhen Angel of Serenity leaves the battlefield, return the exiled cards to their owners' hands.", "Flying\\nWhen Dark Revenant dies, put it on top of its owner's library.", "Flying\\nWhen Faerie Impostor enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you return another creature you control to its owner's hand.", "Flying\\nWhen Isperia's Skywatch enters the battlefield, detain target creature an opponent controls. (Until your next turn, that creature can't attack or block and its activated abilities can't be activated.)", "Flying\\nWhen Lyev Skyknight enters the battlefield, detain target nonland permanent an opponent controls. (Until your next turn, that permanent can't attack or block and its activated abilities can't be activated.)", 'Flying\\nWhen Runewing dies, draw a card.', "Flying\\nWhenever Archon of the Triumvirate attacks, detain up to two target nonland permanents your opponents control. (Until your next turn, those permanents can't attack or block and their activated abilities can't be activated.)", 'Flying\\nWhenever Niv-Mizzet, Dracogenius deals damage to a player, you may draw a card.\\n{U}{R}: Niv-Mizzet, Dracogenius deals 1 damage to any target.', "Flying\\nWhenever Skymark Roc attacks, you may return target creature defending player controls with toughness 2 or less to its owner's hand.", 'Flying\\nWhenever a Dragon you control attacks, create a 6/6 red Dragon creature token with flying.', 'Flying\\nWhenever a creature attacks you or a planeswalker you control, you may draw a card.', 'Flying\\nWhenever a creature you control deals combat damage to a player, put that many +1/+1 counters on it.', 'Flying\\n{W}: Tower Drake gets +0/+1 until end of turn.', 'Gain control of target creature until end of turn. Untap that creature. Until end of turn, it gets +2/+0 and gains haste.', 'Golgari Guildgate enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {G}.', 'Haste', "Haste\\nScavenge {3}{B}{G} ({3}{B}{G}, Exile this card from your graveyard: Put a number of +1/+1 counters equal to this card's power on target creature. Scavenge only as a sorcery.)", "Hexproof (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)", 'If an instant or sorcery card would be put into a graveyard from anywhere, exile it instead.', 'If one or more +1/+1 counters would be put on a creature you control, twice that many +1/+1 counters are put on it instead.', 'Instant and sorcery spells you cast cost {1} less to cast.', 'Izzet Guildgate enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {R}.', "Jarad, Golgari Lich Lord gets +1/+1 for each creature card in your graveyard.\\n{1}{B}{G}, Sacrifice another creature: Each opponent loses life equal to the sacrificed creature's power.\\nSacrifice a Swamp and a Forest: Return Jarad from your graveyard to your hand.", 'Lands you control have "{T}: Add one mana of any color."\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.', 'Lifelink (Damage dealt by this creature also causes you to gain that much life.)', 'Lifelink, haste', "Mana Bloom enters the battlefield with X charge counters on it.\\nRemove a charge counter from Mana Bloom: Add one mana of any color. Activate only once each turn.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if Mana Bloom has no charge counters on it, return it to its owner's hand.", 'Mizzium Mortars deals 4 damage to target creature you don\'t control.\\nOverload {3}{R}{R}{R} (You may cast this spell for its overload cost. If you do, change "target" in its text to "each.")', "Pack Rat's power and toughness are each equal to the number of Rats you control.\\n{2}{B}, Discard a card: Create a token that's a copy of Pack Rat.", "Players can't gain life.\\nAt the beginning of each player's upkeep, that player loses half their life, rounded up.", "Populate. Creatures you control gain indestructible until end of turn. (To populate, create a token that's a copy of a creature token you control.)", "Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt to you this turn. Populate. (Create a token that's a copy of a creature token you control.)", 'Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.\\nPut a +1/+1 counter on target creature.', 'Rakdos Guildgate enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {R}.', "Rakdos's Return deals X damage to target opponent or planeswalker. That player or that planeswalker's controller discards X cards.", 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)', 'Reach, trample', 'Return target card from your graveyard to your hand. Exile Treasured Find.', "Return target creature to its owner's hand. You gain 2 life.", 'Return target nonland permanent you don\'t control to its owner\'s hand.\\nOverload {6}{U} (You may cast this spell for its overload cost. If you do, change "target" in its text to "each.")', 'Reveal the top five cards of your library. You may put a creature or land card from among them into your hand. Put the rest into your graveyard.', 'Sacrifice Keening Apparition: Destroy target enchantment.', "Scavenge {0} ({0}, Exile this card from your graveyard: Put a number of +1/+1 counters equal to this card's power on target creature. Scavenge only as a sorcery.)", "Scavenge {4}{G}{G} ({4}{G}{G}, Exile this card from your graveyard: Put a number of +1/+1 counters equal to this card's power on target creature. Scavenge only as a sorcery.)", "Scavenge {5}{G} ({5}{G}, Exile this card from your graveyard: Put a number of +1/+1 counters equal to this card's power on target creature. Scavenge only as a sorcery.)", "Scavenge {6}{B} ({6}{B}, Exile this card from your graveyard: Put a number of +1/+1 counters equal to this card's power on target creature. Scavenge only as a sorcery.)", 'Search your library for an instant card with mana value 3, reveal it, and put it into your hand. Then repeat this process for instant cards with mana values 2 and 1. Then shuffle.', 'Search your library for up to three basic land cards, reveal them, put them into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for up to two creature cards and reveal them. Put one into your hand and the other into your graveyard. Then shuffle.', 'Selesnya Guildgate enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {W}.', 'Shuffle all cards from your graveyard into your library. Target player mills that many cards.', 'Skull Rend deals 2 damage to each opponent. Those players each discard two cards at random.', "Soulsworn Spirit can't be blocked.\\nWhen Soulsworn Spirit enters the battlefield, detain target creature an opponent controls. (Until your next turn, that creature can't attack or block and its activated abilities can't be activated.)", 'Street Spasm deals X damage to target creature without flying you don\'t control.\\nOverload {X}{X}{R}{R} (You may cast this spell for its overload cost. If you do, change "target" in its text to "each.")', "Swampwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Swamp.)\\nScavenge {2}{B} ({2}{B}, Exile this card from your graveyard: Put a number of +1/+1 counters equal to this card's power on target creature. Scavenge only as a sorcery.)", 'Tap target creature you don\'t control.\\nOverload {3}{U} (You may cast this spell for its overload cost. If you do, change "target" in its text to "each.")', 'Target creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn. Untap that creature.', 'Target creature gets +3/+3 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +3/+3 until end of turn. Another target creature gets -3/-3 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +4/-4 until end of turn.', 'Target creature you control gets +0/+1 and gains hexproof until end of turn.\\nOverload {1}{U} (You may cast this spell for its overload cost. If you do, change "target" in its text to "each.")', 'Target creature you control gets +1/+0 until end of turn and can\'t be blocked this turn.\\nOverload {3}{U}{R} (You may cast this spell for its overload cost. If you do, change "target" in its text to "each.")', 'Target creature you control gets +2/+0 until end of turn.\\nOverload {2}{R} (You may cast this spell for its overload cost. If you do, change "target" in its text to "each.")', 'Target creature you don\'t control gets -2/-0 until end of turn and attacks this turn if able.\\nOverload {3}{U}{R} (You may cast this spell for its overload cost. If you do, change "target" in its text to "each.")', 'Target creature you don\'t control gets -4/-0 until end of turn.\\nOverload {2}{U} (You may cast this spell for its overload cost. If you do, change "target" in its text to "each.")', 'Target player discards two cards.', 'Target player draws two cards.', 'Target player gains 7 life.', "Target player reveals their hand. You gain life equal to the number of cards in that player's hand.", "This spell can't be countered.\\nChoose a nonland card name. Search target opponent's graveyard, hand, and library for any number of cards with that name and exile them. Then that player shuffles.", 'This spell can\'t be countered.\\nCounter target spell you don\'t control.\\nOverload {1}{U}{U}{R} (You may cast this spell for its overload cost. If you do, change "target" in its text to "each.")', "This spell can't be countered.\\nDestroy all creatures.", "This spell can't be countered.\\nDestroy target nonland permanent with mana value 3 or less.", "This spell can't be countered.\\nIf a spell or ability an opponent controls causes you to discard Loxodon Smiter, put it onto the battlefield instead of putting it into your graveyard.", 'Trample\\nCryptborn Horror enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it, where X is the total life lost by your opponents this turn.', 'Trample\\nDiscard a creature card: Put a +1/+1 counter on Lotleth Troll.\\n{B}: Regenerate Lotleth Troll.', "Trample\\nScavenge {5}{G}{G} ({5}{G}{G}, Exile this card from your graveyard: Put a number of +1/+1 counters equal to this card's power on target creature. Scavenge only as a sorcery.)", "Trample\\nUnleash (You may have this creature enter the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. It can't block as long as it has a +1/+1 counter on it.)", 'Trample\\nVolatile Rig attacks each combat if able.\\nWhenever Volatile Rig is dealt damage, flip a coin. If you lose the flip, sacrifice Volatile Rig.\\nWhen Volatile Rig dies, flip a coin. If you lose the flip, it deals 4 damage to each creature and each player.', 'Trample\\nWhen Armada Wurm enters the battlefield, create a 5/5 green Wurm creature token with trample.', "Trample\\nWhen Worldspine Wurm dies, create three 5/5 green Wurm creature tokens with trample.\\nWhen Worldspine Wurm is put into a graveyard from anywhere, shuffle it into its owner's library.", 'Transguild Promenade enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Transguild Promenade enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you pay {1}.\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.', "Unleash (You may have this creature enter the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. It can't block as long as it has a +1/+1 counter on it.)", "Unleash (You may have this creature enter the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. It can't block as long as it has a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\n{1}{B}: Regenerate Grim Roustabout.", "Unleash (You may have this creature enter the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. It can't block as long as it has a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\n{2}{B}{R}, Sacrifice Hellhole Flailer: Hellhole Flailer deals damage equal to its power to target player or planeswalker.", 'Until end of turn, target creature gets +1/+0 and gains first strike and lifelink.', 'Until end of turn, target creature gets +1/+1 for each creature you control and gains trample.', 'Vigilance', "Wayfaring Temple's power and toughness are each equal to the number of creatures you control.\\nWhenever Wayfaring Temple deals combat damage to a player, populate. (Create a token that's a copy of a creature token you control.)", "When Azorius Arrester enters the battlefield, detain target creature an opponent controls. (Until your next turn, that creature can't attack or block and its activated abilities can't be activated.)", "When Azorius Justiciar enters the battlefield, detain up to two target creatures your opponents control. (Until your next turn, those creatures can't attack or block and their activated abilities can't be activated.)", 'When Batterhorn enters the battlefield, you may destroy target artifact.', 'When Centaur Healer enters the battlefield, you gain 3 life.', "When Detention Sphere enters the battlefield, you may exile target nonland permanent not named Detention Sphere and all other permanents with the same name as that permanent.\\nWhen Detention Sphere leaves the battlefield, return the exiled cards to the battlefield under their owner's control.", 'When Drainpipe Vermin dies, you may pay {B}. If you do, target player discards a card.', 'When Rest in Peace enters the battlefield, exile all graveyards.\\nIf a card or token would be put into a graveyard from anywhere, exile it instead.', "When Search the City enters the battlefield, exile the top five cards of your library.\\nWhenever you play a card with the same name as one of the exiled cards, you may put one of those cards with that name into its owner's hand. Then if there are no cards exiled with Search the City, sacrifice it. If you do, take an extra turn after this one.", 'When Seller of Songbirds enters the battlefield, create a 1/1 white Bird creature token with flying.', 'When Slum Reaper enters the battlefield, each player sacrifices a creature.', 'When Viashino Racketeer enters the battlefield, you may discard a card. If you do, draw a card.', "When Voidwielder enters the battlefield, you may return target creature to its owner's hand.", 'Whenever Bazaar Krovod attacks, another target attacking creature gets +0/+2 until end of turn. Untap that creature.', 'Whenever Crosstown Courier deals combat damage to a player, that player mills that many cards.', 'Whenever Stealer of Secrets deals combat damage to a player, draw a card.', 'Whenever Street Sweeper attacks, destroy all Auras attached to target land.', "Whenever Wild Beastmaster attacks, each other creature you control gets +X/+X until end of turn, where X is Wild Beastmaster's power.", 'Whenever a creature you control dies, put X +1/+1 counters on target creature you control, where X is the power of the creature that died.', "Whenever a creature you don't control dies, return it to the battlefield under your control with an additional +1/+1 counter on it at the beginning of the next end step. That creature is a black Zombie in addition to its other colors and types.", "Whenever another creature enters the battlefield under your control, you gain life equal to that creature's toughness.\\n{1}{G}{W}, {T}: Populate. (Create a token that's a copy of a creature token you control.)", 'Whenever you cast a multicolored spell, Pyroconvergence deals 2 damage to any target.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, Blistercoil Weird gets +1/+1 until end of turn. Untap it.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, Guttersnipe deals 2 damage to each opponent.', "You can't cast this spell unless an opponent lost life this turn.\\nFlying, trample\\nCreature spells you cast cost {1} less to cast for each 1 life your opponents have lost this turn.", 'You gain X life and draw X cards.', "[+1]: Until your next turn, whenever a creature an opponent controls attacks, it gets -1/-0 until end of turn.\\n[−2]: Reveal the top three cards of your library. An opponent separates those cards into two piles. Put one pile into your hand and the other on the bottom of your library in any order.\\n[−8]: For each player, search that player's library for a nonland card and exile it, then that player shuffles. You may cast those cards without paying their mana costs.", '[+1]: Until your next turn, whenever a creature deals combat damage to Vraska the Unseen, destroy that creature.\\n[−3]: Destroy target nonland permanent.\\n[−7]: Create three 1/1 black Assassin creature tokens with "Whenever this creature deals combat damage to a player, that player loses the game."', '{1}{B}: Perilous Shadow gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', "{1}{B}{G}: Target creature gets +1/+1 and gains intimidate until end of turn. (It can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or creatures that share a color with it.)\\n{2}{B}{G}, Sacrifice a nontoken creature: Create X 1/1 green Saproling creature tokens, where X is the sacrificed creature's toughness.", '{1}{R}: Bellows Lizard gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', '{1}{U}{R}: Draw a card, then discard a card.\\n{2}{U}{R}: Copy target instant or sorcery spell you control. You may choose new targets for the copy.', '{2}{B}: Stonefare Crocodile gains lifelink until end of turn. (Damage dealt by this creature also causes you to gain that much life.)', "{2}{G}, Sacrifice Centaur's Herald: Create a 3/3 green Centaur creature token.", '{2}{U}, {T}: Target creature gets -2/-0 until end of turn.', "{4}{G}{W}: Create a 3/3 green Centaur creature token.\\n{2}{G}{W}: Populate. (Create a token that's a copy of a creature token you control.)", '{5}{G}: Regenerate Selesnya Sentry.', '{B}{R}: Target blocking creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.\\n{B}{R}: Target player who lost life this turn loses 1 life.', '{G}, Sacrifice another creature: Put a +1/+1 counter on Gobbling Ooze.', '{T}, Pay 3 life: Flip a coin. If you win the flip, you gain 6 life.', '{T}: Add {B} or {G}.\\n{B}{G}: Golgari Keyrune becomes a 2/2 black and green Insect artifact creature with deathtouch until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {B} or {R}.\\n{B}{R}: Rakdos Keyrune becomes a 3/1 black and red Devil artifact creature with first strike until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{3}{G}{W}, {T}, Tap two untapped creatures you control, Sacrifice Grove of the Guardian: Create an 8/8 green and white Elemental creature token with vigilance.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{4}, {T}: Target creature can't be blocked this turn.", '{T}: Add {G} or {W}.\\n{G}{W}: Selesnya Keyrune becomes a 3/3 green and white Wolf artifact creature until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {U} or {R}.\\n{U}{R}: Until end of turn, Izzet Keyrune becomes a 2/1 blue and red Elemental artifact creature.\\nWhenever Izzet Keyrune deals combat damage to a player, you may draw a card. If you do, discard a card.', '{T}: Add {W} or {U}.\\n{W}{U}: Azorius Keyrune becomes a 2/2 white and blue Bird artifact creature with flying until end of turn.', '{T}: Exile target land card from a graveyard. Add one mana of any color.\\n{B}, {T}: Exile target instant or sorcery card from a graveyard. Each opponent loses 2 life.\\n{G}, {T}: Exile target creature card from a graveyard. You gain 2 life.', '{T}: Target player mills a card. (They put the top card of their library into their graveyard.)\\n{5}, {T}, Sacrifice Codex Shredder: Return target card from your graveyard to your hand.', '{U/R}: Frostburn Weird gets +1/-1 until end of turn.', "{U}, {T}: Draw two cards.\\n{R}, {T}, Discard a card: Mercurial Chemister deals damage to target creature equal to the discarded card's mana value.", "{W}{U}: Target creature gains flying until end of turn.\\n{3}{W}{U}: Detain target nonland permanent an opponent controls. (Until your next turn, that permanent can't attack or block and its activated abilities can't be activated.)"]
flavor: ['"A kick from its hooves is like a bolt of lightning. I\'d know. I\'ve been hit by both."\\n—Rencz, Izzet chemister\'s aide', '"And would you care to explain why your satchel is radiating an aura of unstable energy?"', '"Civilization will subsume us unless we overwhelm it instead."\\n—Speaker Zegana', '"Day 31: I finally succeeded in my time reversal experiment!\\n"Day 30: I might have a problem here."\\n—Journal of the Prime Izmagnus', '"Even this primitive specimen of my kind is impressive."\\n—Niv-Mizzet', '"Finally, a weapon the Boros can\'t confiscate!"\\n—Juri, proprietor of the Juri Revue', '"For each griffin wounded by an arrow, there\'s a corpse with a bow nearby."\\n—Pel Javya, Wojek investigator', '"Forgive the theft. Punish the deception."\\n—Alcarus, Selesnya archer', '"Give me enough refuse and mana and I will summon an ooze that can engulf all of Ravnica."\\n—Cevraya, Golgari shaman', '"Having conviction is more important than being righteous."\\n—Aurelia', '"He makes up his own laws, and that\'s dangerous to all who love peace and prosperity. Kill him on sight."\\n—Mirela, Azorius hussar', '"I never thought I\'d be so glad to see two tons of beak and claws bearing down on me at the speed of an arrow."\\n—Mirela, Azorius hussar', '"I serve only justice. But through that duty, I serve all of Ravnica."', '"I\'ve dreamt of the future, Isperia. Danger is on the horizon. You must heed my warning."', '"If there were such a thing as a soul, I think it would be behind the gallbladder but above the kidneys."', '"If this is thinking, I don\'t know what I was doing before."', '"In each of us is the strength of all of us."\\n—Trostani', '"In troubled times, we all need someone to watch our back."', '"It is forbidden. Asking why is irrelevant."\\n—Sergiu, Opal Lake magistrate', '"It makes better use of Uncle Dragi\'s head than he ever did."\\n—Pesha, retired blacksmith', '"It misses nothing and it has no sense of humor."\\n—Barvisa, courtroom scribe', '"It will dodge your first arrow and flatten you before there\'s a second."\\n—Alcarus, Selesnya archer', '"Jarad fancies himself king of the undercity, but he\'s merely king of rot."', '"Lady Wren is the one merchant in Keyhole Downs who isn\'t running a scam."\\n—Mirela, Azorius hussar', '"Let all feel joy in pain."\\n—Rakdos', '"Let him be an example to others who would default on their debts to us."\\n—"The Cozen," Orzhov assassin', '"Let the knowledge of absolute law inspire you to live a life of absolute order."', '"Let the rest of Ravnica sneer. One way or another, they all end up in the undercity."\\n—Jarad', '"My ruling is final. Order is upheld. Justice is done."', '"Obviously, the Firemind\'s mission is worth more than a few goblins."\\n—Pelener, chamberlain of Niv-Mizzet', '"One day every pillar will be a tree and every hall a glade."\\n—Trostani', '"Patience, mage. Killing you now would be too easy."', '"Preachers of freedom forget that conformity can be beautiful."', '"Smarter than death? Let\'s see you outsmart my mace, necromancer!"', '"So many oppose us, but we are the reed that bends without breaking."', '"Some cannot be saved as they are, but all can serve the Worldsoul."\\n—Trostani', '"Straight from the blood-drenched imagination of our illustrious parun!"\\n—Nyoser, Gore-House ringleader', '"Such boorish noise is what passes for subtlety among the Boros."\\n—Vraska', '"The Izzet are an equation that turns lunacy into explosions."\\n—Leonos, Azorius arbiter', '"The Izzet are searching for something. Discern what or die trying."', '"The Selesnya are gathering armies. Do you still believe they aren\'t preparing for war?"\\n—Teysa, to Isperia', '"The entire murder scene was covered in dripping, oozing slime. No need for a soothsayer to solve that one."\\n—Pel Javya, Wojek investigator', '"The good of society matters much more than the inconvenience of a few."\\n—Agmand Sarv, Azorius hussar', '"The higher the mind soars, the greater its understanding of the law."\\n—Isperia', '"The most impressive performances can be done only once."\\n—Mote, Rakdos madcap', '"The only action worth taking is one with an unknown outcome."', '"The other guilds will learn the hard way not to interfere with our investigations."\\n—Bori Andon, Izzet blastseeker', '"The prohibition of unnecessary tossing of the citizenry by giants shall also extend to spontaneous giants."\\n—Isperia\'s Edict, provision VII.789.2', '"The rules of logic and order have already made the choice for you."\\n—Isperia', '"To prevent action is to prevent transgression."\\n—Azorius Arrester motto', '"Try not to look guilty. Or delicious."\\n—Thorpe, street urchin', '"Watch the voltage. We don\'t need another charred, crashing viashino."\\n—Bori Andon, Izzet blastseeker', '"We can\'t control enemies who have no regard for their own survival."\\n—Arrester Lavinia, Tenth Precinct', '"We could never accept anyone with a face that pretty or a mind that sane."\\n—Nyoser, Gore-House ringleader', '"We follow it through its tunnels, and where it dies, we farm."\\n—Mihas, spore druid', '"We traffic in flesh, not souls. Still, it\'s a shame to let anything go to waste."\\n—Cevraya, Golgari shaman', '"We will defend the Worldsoul from Izzet \'progress\' at any cost."', '"We will grow an army large enough to withstand the Izzet\'s madness."\\n—Trostani', '"We will prove your guilt. We don\'t arrest the innocent, you know."\\n—Arrester Lavinia, Tenth Precinct', '"What root and branch cannot reach, our winged friends will attend to."\\n—Zunak, Selesnya strategist', '"When the spires have burned and the cobblestones are dust, he will take his rightful place as king of the wilds."\\n—Kirce, Axebane guardian', '"When they covered the world in city, all they did was give themselves nowhere to run."', '"Without a body, the soul is helpless to fight the terms of our contracts."\\n—Somhaur, Orzhov pontiff', '"You have the right to remain silent. Mostly because I tire of your excuses."', '"You just need the right incentive to fulfill my dreams."', '"You may call me a fool, selling this stuff on Orzhov turf. Well, you need to be a little reckless to survive."', '"You think no one is watching, you think you\'re smart enough to escape, and most foolish of all, you think no one cares."\\n—Arrester Lavinia, Tenth Precinct', '"Your potential to commit a crime warrants further investigation."', 'A bargain in Keyhole Downs is always too good to be true.', "A gargoyle's voice reaches pitches that will shatter glass and warp bone.", 'A mark of unity when you want one; a fierce guardian when you need one.', 'A place to relax, if you have the proper permit.', 'After his death, the general was reunited with fallen soldiers from over thirty of his campaigns.', 'Although Cryptwitch Merree vanished after a spat with Rakdos, her playthings lingered.', 'An elocutor forces criminals to confess to the laws they merely intended to break.', 'As the bounty on Massacre Girl rose, so did the number of imitators.', 'As the price of wood and coal rose, smiths found creative ways to keep their forges burning.', 'As whispers and rumors increased, so did the demand for fail-safe barriers.', "Azorius lawmages would like to outlaw the creation of weirds, but first they'd have to settle their long-standing debate on how to classify them.", 'Beauty is in the eye of the exploder.', "Bleak rumors reached Trostani's ears. She decreed that no one should travel alone.", 'Centaurs are sent to evangelize in Gruul territories where words of war speak louder than prayers of peace.', 'Close finishes are settled by who can dismount and get to weapons first.', 'Crafted with genius, energized with madness.', 'Despite its enormous stature, it can fold itself into a tunnel with startling quickness, vanishing back into the undercity.', 'Devil-blades and dripping blood make music Rakdos never tires of hearing.', 'Dimir mages put the lanterns to good use, creating shapeshifters and sleeper agents from mana foreign to them.', "Don't cross a Devkarin elf unless you long for an early grave.", 'Enter and indulge your darkest fantasies, for you may never pass this way again.', 'Enter and rejoice! The Conclave stands united, open to one and all.', 'Enter the Senate, the seat of justice and the foundation of Ravnican society.', 'Enter those who are starving and sick. You are welcome among the Swarm when the rest of Ravnica rejects you.', 'Enter those with the vision to create and the daring to release their creations.', 'Every inch of Ravnica is home to something.', 'Everyone knew the Dimir had done the damage. Everyone suspected the Izzet had hired them.', 'For the Azorius, the opportunity to serve the law is too great an honor for death to interrupt.', 'Goblins and architects seldom get along.', 'Gorgons crave beautiful things: gems, exquisite amulets, the alabaster corpses of the petrified dead . . .', 'Gruul warriors never need to be stirred to battle. They need only to be shown where the battle is.', 'He has no patience for minds that do not inspire him or explode by trying.', 'He lurks in the undercity, eager for the corpse haulers to unload their rotting cargo.', 'He wants to watch Ravnica burn, one soul at a time.', "He'll point you to your death row seats.", "He's the unlife of the party.", 'His prowess gives the guildless hope that they can hold out against tyranny.', "If the pig's blood drips on you, you're next on the chain.", "If you're looking for it, it's available. The question is how much you're willing to pay.", 'In Rakdos-controlled neighborhoods, everyone is part of the show.', 'In the gardens of the Conclave, order and beauty are the roots of power.', 'In the hands of the open-minded, a runewing quill writes wisdom of its own.', 'In the towering trees of the Samok Stand and the predators that guard them, the might of the Ravnican wild has returned.', "In water, it's as graceful as a dolphin. On land, it darts and jerks so unpredictably that few can ride it for long.", "Information travels quickly through Ravnica's network of messengers and thought agents.", 'Insatiable, irresistible, and insane.', 'Instructors at the Kasarna training grounds are capable healers in case their students fail to grasp the subtleties of combat.', 'It chases its airborne prey relentlessly, heedless to what it pulverizes beneath its hooves.', 'It is rumored the Azorius paid an exorbitant sum to ensure its symbol would appear at the top.', 'It took three years for it to occur to him to use the chain as a weapon, but once it did, he made up for lost time.', "It's easier to just aim at everything.", "It's sent into unguilded districts by the Orzhov to collect the souls of those no one will miss.", 'Its favorite treats are candied hands and sweet hearts.', "Joining the Worldsoul took years of study and meditation. Severing that connection took the snap of Rakdos's fingers.", "Leonos had no second thoughts about the abolishment edict. He'd left skyrunes warning of the eviction, even though it was cloudy.", "Life's too short to not do the things you love.", 'Like a single ant, it only hints at the colony below.', 'Magistrate Ludy agreed to designate land for the brushstriders only after several broken windows and dozens of missing blini-cakes.', 'Many Tin Street shops display a sign on the door: "No cloaks allowed."', 'Many chemisters are oblivious to the innumerable machinations of their guild, instead focusing obsessively on creating the perfect weird.', 'Metal is scarce, smiths are pricey, and plate mail is heavy.', 'No one in the Conclave acts alone.', 'Nothing evens the odds like a little lightning.', 'Nothing was going to stop it—not the narrow alleys, not the Boros garrison, and certainly not the four-story Orzhov cathedral.', 'Novice shopkeeps spend hours deciding how best to display their wares. Veterans focus on portability.', 'One of the many reasons why open-air markets close at dusk.', 'One piercing stare usually convinces thieves to go elsewhere.', 'Only a worthy few are permitted within the sentient forest known as Axebane.', 'Ragemutts pull the chariots of the Butcher Clowns, a trio of wingless, zombified faeries formerly of the Izzet.', 'Rakdos cultists are her best customers. They never flinch at pain and are seldom good at math.', "Raked by vertical spikes of glass and stone, Ravnica's vistas offer only a rare glimpse of the horizon.", 'Ravnicans still tell tales about the Battle of Sumala where four Selesnya sentries held off an entire clan of Gruul warriors.', "Refusing guild allegiances, she fights for those who can't protect themselves.", 'Rumors quickly spread among thieves about a labyrinth without walls and a prize beyond all measures of worth.', 'Senators of Azorius often hired agents to spy on the Selesnya. They were told to record every spore and root they saw, as each could become a deadly foe.', 'Some Golgari insects live for centuries—and they never stop growing.', 'Some Ravnicans consider carrying a sword to be beneath them, preferring instead a tooth-and-claw escort.', 'Some corpses the Golgari cannot claim. Some souls the Orzhov cannot shackle.', 'Some souls are too damaged to be of use to the Orzhov.', 'The Dimir agents watched from the shadows. "Eight hours, and I\'ve yet to see him blink," Nefara hissed. "I suggest we find another way in."', 'The Dimir would hire her, if only they knew where she lived. The Azorius would condemn her, if only they knew her name.', "The Hauler's Collective wields great influence over the Ravnican merchant class. Without it, little moves in the city.", 'The Izzet quickly suspended their policy of lifetime guarantees.', 'The Izzet specialize in unnatural disaster.', "The Izzet's plans to exploit the undercity ran into a few stubborn obstacles.", 'The Rakdos believe that all are eager to join their revels, even when told otherwise.', 'The Rakdos use it for everything you can think of and plenty more than that.', "The Street Swarm is the labor class that drives the Golgari's endless cycle of life and death.", 'The best funeral shroud is the fabric of new life.', 'The city is vast and perilous, but there are places where a weary traveler can feel very much at home.', 'The farther they go from Vitu-Ghazi, the less willing the crowd is to part for them.', 'The fear of dragons is as old and as powerful as the fear of death itself.', 'The fearful want the procedure before a blood festival. The guilty seek it afterward.', 'The first motion put forth in the pristine Jelenn Column was for severe restrictions on the airspace around New Prahv.', 'The furious citizens blamed the Simic for releasing it in their district. The Simic pointed out that rats were no longer a problem.', "The mask isn't meant to hide his identity. It's meant to keep the viscera out of his eyes.", 'The most ancient streets take on a life of their own. A few have decided to move to nicer neighborhoods.', 'The murderer faced justice in the Azorius courts, but his soul was set free on a technicality.', 'The ruins of Old Prahv became a wildspace, although all birdsong was silenced by lingering Azorius magic.', 'The silk of the archweavers adds structural integrity to otherwise unstable Izzet building sites.', 'The smelting district is home to many who see the guilds as not for them.', 'The star performer of the Juri Revue, his shows have fans and blood spilling into the street.', 'The sweepers roam endlessly, scrubbing away the refuse—and anything else too slow or too clumsy to get out of their way.', "The trouble started when a street urchin bet a goblin he could ride one until the clock on Shilbo's Tower struck thirteen.", 'There are some shadows that even the Dimir fear.', 'They share no bloodline, but a bond greater than family unites them. Such are the gifts of the Worldsoul.', 'Those without a guild signet often display a different form of protection.', 'To the Golgari, anything buried is treasure.', 'Unwelcome in Golgari colonies, he found his own dark place from which to represent the Swarm.', 'Weakness is not in the nature of the Swarm.', 'Weather is more predictable than the Izzet.', 'What some see as "distracted" is really "fathoming the unfathomable."', "When Lord Rakdos stirred from his slumber, everyone else's nightmare began.", 'When Selesnya missionaries moved into the Shanav Quarter, they faced scorn, ridicule, and ultimately martyrdom.', 'When asked how much power is required, Izzet mages always answer "more."', 'When it escaped, the experimenters hesitated. It would cause untold havoc, yet they wished to see it in action.', 'When one of the great guardians arises, it sweeps enemies aside like chaff yet takes care not to crush a single insect underfoot.', 'When times are tough, the poor eat the rats. When times are tougher, the rats eat the poor.', 'Where the dead serve as diversion, decor, and dessert.', 'With no memories left to compare to his present situation, Andalum was finally content.', 'With the Izzet occupied elsewhere, many of their public works fell into disrepair.', 'Wolf riders hone their skills traversing the perilous rooftops, each dizzying step bringing elf and wolf closer together.', "You don't so much hire goblins as put ideas in their heads."]
artist: ['Adam Paquette', 'Aleksi Briclot', 'Anthony Palumbo', 'BD', 'Chase Stone', 'Chippy', 'Chris Rahn', 'Christine Choi', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Cliff Childs', 'Clint Cearley', 'Cynthia Sheppard', 'Daarken', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daniel Ljunggren', 'Dave Kendall', 'David Palumbo', 'David Rapoza', 'Drew Baker', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Eric Velhagen', 'Eytan Zana', 'Greg Staples', 'Howard Lyon', 'Izzy', 'Jack Wang', 'Jaime Jones', 'James Ryman', 'Jason Chan', 'Jason Felix', 'Johann Bodin', 'Johannes Voss', 'John Avon', 'Jung Park', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Kev Walker', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Lucas Graciano', 'Marco Nelor', 'Mark Zug', 'Martina Pilcerova', 'Mathias Kollros', 'Matt Stewart', 'Michael C. Hayes', 'Mike Bierek', 'Min Yum', 'Nic Klein', 'Nils Hamm', 'Noah Bradley', 'Peter Mohrbacher', 'Raoul Vitale', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Richard Wright', 'Ryan Barger', 'Ryan Pancoast', 'Sam Burley', 'Scott Chou', 'Scott M. Fischer', 'Seb McKinnon', 'Slawomir Maniak', 'Steve Argyle', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Todd Lockwood', 'Tomasz Jedruszek', 'Trevor Claxton', 'Tyler Jacobson', 'Vincent Proce', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Warren Mahy', 'Wayne Reynolds', 'Wesley Burt', 'Willian Murai', 'Winona Nelson', 'Yeong-Hao Han', 'Zoltan Boros']
